`bmb check` does not report the diagnostic E0607 yet: `pure` listed with another effect, or an effect listed twice. It came with the commit "2F-02, 2F-03 (ADR-0030), 2E-02..2E-04 (ADR-0029): effect sets with alloc and panic; escapes with rationales and trust levels". Implement it. Examples of what `bmb check` must print (one JSON line per diagnostic; the path in `file` is the one given on the command line), each after the source line it points at:

    #[effects(pure, io)]
    {"code": "E0607", "severity": "error", "message": "`pure` means no effect: it cannot be listed with `io`", "file": "err/effects.bmb", "line": 9, "col": 5, "end_line": 9, "end_col": 25, "fix": {"message": "write `#[effects(io)]`", "replacement": "#[effects(io)]"}}

    #[effects(io, io)]
    {"code": "E0607", "severity": "error", "message": "an effect is listed twice", "file": "err/effects.bmb", "line": 66, "col": 5, "end_line": 66, "end_col": 23, "fix": {"message": "write `#[effects(io)]`", "replacement": "#[effects(io)]"}}

Everything else the program prints must stay as it is.

